    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d658">

                <pb facs="0911" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/432: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-21T10:00:00-06:00">February 21, 1931—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1: 50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>39. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation at Managua: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>February 21, 9 a.m. Your February 20, 4 p.m. Under instructions of the
                            Department action was taken by me in accordance with paragraph 3 of
                            Department’s telegram No. 19, February 19, 5 p.m., to you before I
                            received your telegram of February 20, 1 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >4</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="15a" xml:id="d658-f1"/> President of Honduras
                            accepted my informal suggestion and issued statement to press as
                            follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                                <p>“The Government of Honduras will increase its regular forces now
                                    patrolling our Nicaraguan frontier to the proportions necessary
                                        <pb facs="0912" n="798" xml:id="pg798"/> to provide complete
                                    protection for the Commission against any attack of the
                                    malefactors”.</p>
                            </quote></p>
                        <p>This statement was published this afternoon in local newspaper as a reply
                            to a question in an interview with a reporter. The Honduran Chargé at
                            Managua has been instructed to communicate it to the Nicaraguan
                            Government also.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d658-f1" n="15a" xml:id="d658-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 35, from the Minister in Nicaragua, <hi rendition="#italic"
